  ],
  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Krokeai. According to the Oxford Roman Economy Project, this quarry was a source of a dark green serpentine known either as porfido verde di Grecia or serpentino. This stone was used from the Late Bronze Age (Mycenaeans) to the Roman Imperial period.</p>",
